{
  "title": "AC1021 SOLID/TRACE absent string marker",
  "authority": "ODA DWG v5.4.1 \u00a720.1 locates the R2007+ string-present bit immediately before handles; \u00a7\u00a720.4.35\u201336 define SOLID/TRACE thickness, shared elevation, four OCS corners and extrusion.",
  "problem": "The AC1021 writer aligned empty-string entity bodies without first writing the absent-string bit. Tilted SOLID/TRACE with zero thickness end their scalar fields on a byte boundary; their handles therefore start before the required marker. LibreDWG reports -1 OVERSHOOT and ODA fails at the entity.",
  "physical_source": "ezdxf 1.4.5 authored eight AC1021 DXFs (SOLID/TRACE \u00d7 +Z/+Y normal \u00d7 zero/.5 thickness), each with a following LINE; ODA File Converter 27.1 produced AC1021 DWGs and returned AC1027 DXFs. Local ODA conversion lineage is observed rather than authenticated by individual hashes.",
  "boundary_evidence": "For both producer tilted/zero examples LibreDWG 0.14 reports scalar extrusion ending at bit 680 and declared handle boundary 681; generated baseline reports boundary 680 and -1 OVERSHOOT. Generated corrected boundary is 688: explicit zero bit followed by padding under the writer\u2019s existing byte-aligned handle framing. Producer\u2019s exact bit boundary and generated padded boundary are distinct.",
  "results": "All eight producer files round-trip. Baseline generated tilted/zero SOLID and TRACE fail at the entity, produce .err and no DXF; baseline other six convert. Corrected generated eight convert without .err; the six non-aligned controls are byte-identical to baseline, while only the two aligned failing files change. Sixteen source/corrected pairs and all eight baseline DWGs passed independent LibreDWG/ezdxf peer audits, including exact normal, thickness, four OCS corners, WCS polygon corners, model BLOCK_HEADER membership, layer references and following LINE. Baseline failing files have no DXF, so only their DWG graph/geometry was audited. All four batch stdout/stderr files are empty; the two baseline .err files contain earlier table warnings as well as the fatal entity diagnostic.",
  "change": "In dwgWriter21::finishObject append the existing absent-string bit for fixed SOLID and TRACE when the string stream is empty; keep handle alignment and all other entity types/versions unchanged.",
  "focused": "ctest --test-dir /private/tmp/face3d-probe/build -R ^libdxfrw_dwg_ac1021_solid_trace_footer$ --output-on-failure passes 1/1. Unmodified source fails the same test. It verifies exact bit boundary and zero marker for both types and four normal/thickness combinations, CRC-valid frames and scalar payloads, native parsing, truncated-body failure/retry, reconstructed historical body parser compatibility, following LINE parsing and failed-EED same-writer retry. The reconstructed historical body check does not claim a resealed full-frame CRC or whole-file historical fixture.",
  "limits": "The physical source and generated outputs are the sampled AC1021 profiles using the existing material and plotstyle opt-ins; no arbitrary normals, native CAD rendering, whole-file interoperability or cross-version qualification is claimed. No fixture files added.",
  "peer_audit_command": "PYTHONPATH=tools <ezdxf-python> -B tools/audit_ac1021_solid_trace_peer.py --dwgread /opt/homebrew/bin/dwgread --dwg <path> --dwg-sha256 <sha> [--dxf <path> --dxf-sha256 <sha>] --entity <SOLID|TRACE> --normal <default|tilt> --thickness <zero|thick> [--generated-graph]",
  "reproduction": [
    "Use tools/author_ac1021_solid_trace.py <new-directory> with ezdxf 1.4.5 to author equivalent source DXFs; metadata and hashes may vary.",
    "Convert source DXFs to ACAD2007 DWG, then ACAD2013 DXF using ODA.",
    "Compile tools/probe_ac1021_solid_trace.cpp against the final library with -std=c++17 and include paths <source>/src, <source>/src/intern, <source>/tests; invoke <producer> <solid|trace>-<default|tilt>-<zero|thick> <new-dwg>, then convert ACAD2013 DXF.",
    "Run the hash-bound peer audit on each exact source, baseline and corrected pair; omit DXF only for the two baseline failures. Wrong-hash refusal is verified under Python -O."
  ],
